IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-types`
IMPORT `sfa-definitions`

-- Sale of Food Act 1973 — GOALS 2-3: OFFENCES, DEFENCES AND PENALTIES
-- (Parts 3, 4 and 7; ss 5-10, 10K, 26, 27, 31-33, 40, 41, 46, 48-50, 56).
--
--   Goal 2: "Does this conduct contravene the Act, and what is the most it
--   can cost (or be compounded for)?"
--   Goal 3: "Does a defence answer it — the reasonable-steps proviso
--   (s 32), the written warranty (s 33), the carrier or publisher (ss 16A(6),
--   40(4)) — and who else is liable (ss 26, 27)?"
--
-- Source: ../source/SFA1973.txt, the sections cited.

§ `Goals 2-3 — offences, defences and penalties`

§§ `The elements`

-- Part 3: "A person must not sell" — s 11 "any adulterated food without fully
-- informing the purchaser ... of the nature of the adulteration"; s 12 food
-- with a prohibited substance; s 13 a substance above the permitted
-- proportion; s 14 "more than 50 parts of methyl alcohol, isopropyl alcohol
-- or denatured alcohol in one million parts"; s 15 food "that the person
-- knows or ought reasonably to know is unsafe" / "unsuitable"; s 16 food not
-- packaged or labelled as required; s 17 food "labelled or advertised in a
-- manner that is false, misleading or deceptive"; s 18 food "not of the
-- quality or not of the nature, or not of the substance of the food demanded";
-- s 19 food prepared "under insanitary conditions". s 20: each is an offence.
-- s 16A(2): a seller or promoter (or its agent or employee) "must not publish"
-- a non-compliant advertisement. s 21: "must not carry on a non-retail food
-- business except in accordance with a licence". s 10K(1), (3); s 40(2);
-- s 41; s 5(4), (5); s 6(4); s 7(2); s 10(3); s 33(5); s 46(6); s 48(3).
@ref ss 5(4)-(5), 6(4), 7(2), 10(3), 10K(1), (3), 11-21, 22(5), 23, 24(1), 33(5), 40(2)-(3), 41, 46(6), 48(3), 56(1)(r)
GIVEN c IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct contravenes the Act` c IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `selling adulterated food` told                               THEN NOT told
    WHEN `selling food with methyl, isopropyl or denatured alcohol` ppm THEN ppm GREATER THAN 50
    WHEN `selling unsafe food` knew                                    THEN knew
    WHEN `selling unsuitable food` knew                                THEN knew
    WHEN `publishing a non-compliant food advertisement` seller carrier excepted THEN seller
    WHEN `carrying on a food business` b                               THEN `a non-retail food business` b AND NOT b's `licensed under Part 4`
    WHEN `giving a false written warranty` believed                    THEN NOT believed
    WHEN `importing, advertising or selling a prohibited food contact article` carrier warned THEN TRUE
    -- s 10K(1): "without reasonable excuse"; (3): "while that direction
    -- remains in force"; s 41(2): "without authority" (obstruction under (1)
    -- needs none, so authority is read as answering only the mark or seal
    -- limb); s 6(3): no one must sell less than a whole unopened package, and
    -- s 7(1)(b): other food only "upon the request or with the consent of the
    -- purchaser". Added after the independent pass.
    WHEN `failing to comply with a food safety direction` excuse         THEN NOT excuse
    WHEN `removing a direction affixed to food premises` inForce         THEN inForce
    WHEN `obstructing an officer, or interfering with an official mark` authorised THEN NOT authorised
    WHEN `refusing to give a sample` lawful                              THEN lawful
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `Defences (ss 16A(6)-(7), 31-33, 40(4)-(5))`

-- s 32: "it is not a defence that the accused did not act wilfully, unless the
-- accused also proves that the accused took all reasonable steps to ascertain
-- that the sale ... would not constitute an offence". It speaks of "a
-- prosecution for selling". s 31: that the purchaser bought for analysis is
-- no defence.
@ref ss 31, 32
GIVEN c IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a prosecution for selling` c IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `publishing a non-compliant food advertisement` a b d        THEN FALSE
    WHEN `carrying on a food business` b                               THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a licensee failing to have staff immunised as required`      THEN FALSE
    WHEN `transporting food in an unclean vehicle, or without required equipment` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `failing to comply with a food safety direction` x              THEN FALSE
    WHEN `removing a direction affixed to food premises` x               THEN FALSE
    WHEN `obstructing an officer, or interfering with an official mark` x THEN FALSE
    WHEN `refusing to give information required by an officer`         THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an officer breaching secrecy`                                THEN FALSE
    WHEN `refusing to give a sample` x                                   THEN FALSE
    WHEN `using an analysis result as an advertisement`                THEN FALSE
    WHEN `giving a false written warranty` b                           THEN FALSE
    WHEN `wilfully giving false information in a licence application`  THEN FALSE
    WHEN `refusing or mis-stating name and address`                    THEN FALSE
    WHEN `contravening food regulations`                               THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Part 3 offences, for s 33(1).
GIVEN c IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Part 3 offence` c IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `selling adulterated food` t                                  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `selling food with a prohibited substance`                    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `selling food with a substance over the permitted proportion` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `selling food with methyl, isopropyl or denatured alcohol` p  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `selling unsafe food` k                                       THEN TRUE
    WHEN `selling unsuitable food` k                                   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `selling food packaged or labelled non-compliantly`           THEN TRUE
    WHEN `publishing a non-compliant food advertisement` a b d         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `selling food falsely or misleadingly labelled or advertised` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `selling food not of the nature, substance or quality demanded, to the purchaser's prejudice` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `selling food prepared under insanitary conditions`           THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 33(1): "a good defence in any prosecution for an offence under Part 3 if
-- the accused proves that — (a) the accused purchased the food ... in
-- reliance on a written warranty or other written statement as to [its]
-- nature ..., signed by or on behalf of the person from whom the accused
-- purchased [it]; (b) the accused had no reason to believe that the food ...
-- did not conform ...; and (c) if the food ... had truly conformed ..., the
-- sale ... would not have constituted the offence". (2): a warrantor resident
-- outside Singapore — only if the accused "had taken reasonable steps to
-- ascertain and did in fact believe in the truth". (3): only if, "within
-- 7 days after service of the summons", the accused delivered to the
-- prosecutor a copy with written notice, and "within the same time" sent the
-- warrantor a like notice by registered post.
@ref s 33(1)-(3)
GIVEN w IS A `Warranty facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the warranty defence is made out` w IF
        w's `bought in reliance on a signed written warranty as to its nature`
    AND w's `no reason to believe the food did not conform`
    AND w's `had it conformed, there would be no offence`
    AND ((NOT w's `the warrantor resides outside Singapore`) OR w's `took reasonable steps and believed the warranty`)
    AND `in time` (w's `notice with a copy delivered to the prosecutor on`)
    AND `in time` (w's `like notice posted to the warrantor on`)
    WHERE
        `in time` d MEANS
            CONSIDER d
            WHEN JUST x  THEN x AT MOST (w's `summons served on`) PLUS 7
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- s 16A(6)-(7), s 40(4)-(5): a carrier with no control over content, or a
-- publisher of advertisements in the ordinary course, has a defence, unless
-- it ought reasonably to have known, had been warned in writing by or for the
-- Director-General, or (s 16A(7)(c) only) is in the food business concerned.
@ref ss 16A(6)-(7), 40(4)-(5)
GIVEN c IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carrier or publisher defence is made out` c IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `publishing a non-compliant food advertisement` seller carrier excepted THEN carrier AND NOT excepted
    WHEN `importing, advertising or selling a prohibited food contact article` carrier warned THEN carrier AND NOT warned
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@ref ss 16A(6)-(7), 31-33, 40(4)-(5)
GIVEN f IS A `Food case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a defence answers the charge` f IF
        `the carrier or publisher defence is made out` (f's `conduct`)
    OR  (`a prosecution for selling` (f's `conduct`) AND f's `did not act wilfully, and took all reasonable steps to ascertain the sale was lawful`)
    OR  (`a Part 3 offence` (f's `conduct`) AND
            CONSIDER f's `warranty`
            WHEN JUST w  THEN `the warranty defence is made out` w
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)

§§ `Who else is liable (ss 26, 27)`

-- s 26: where food in breach is "sold in an unopened package", a person who
-- appears from a statement on it to have imported, manufactured, prepared or
-- packed it "is, unless proved to the contrary, deemed to have so [done] ...
-- and shall be liable to the same fine as if that person had actually sold"
-- it. s 27(b): on a sale by an agent or employee, "the ... principal or
-- employer shall be under the same liability as if the principal or employer
-- had effected the sale personally".
@ref ss 26, 27
GIVEN `unopened package` IS A BOOLEAN, `named on it as importer, maker or packer` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the named importer, maker or packer is liable as seller, unopened package:` `unopened package` `, named:` `named on it as importer, maker or packer` `, proved otherwise:` `proved otherwise` IF
    `unopened package` AND `named on it as importer, maker or packer` AND NOT `proved otherwise`

@ref s 27(b)
GIVEN `sold by an agent or employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the principal or employer is liable as if the seller, sold by an agent or employee:` `sold by an agent or employee` IF
    `sold by an agent or employee`

§§ `Penalties (ss 10K, 48, 49, 50, 56(1)(r))`

DECLARE `SFA penalty` HAS
    `fine`                       IS A NUMBER
    `imprisonment in months`     IS A NUMBER
    `fine per day continuing`    IS A NUMBER

-- s 10K(2): "$10,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months";
-- s 10K(4): "$5,000 or ... 6 months"; s 48(3): "a fine not exceeding $300";
-- s 56(1)(r): regulations may fix "a fine not exceeding $5,000 and, in the
-- case of a continuing offence, a further fine of $500 for every day";
-- s 49: otherwise "a fine not exceeding $5,000 and, in the case of a second or
-- subsequent conviction, ... $10,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not
-- exceeding 3 months or ... both".
@ref ss 10K(2), (4), 48(3), 49, 56(1)(r)
GIVEN c IS A Conduct, repeat IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `SFA penalty`
`the maximum penalty for` c `, a second or subsequent conviction:` repeat MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `failing to comply with a food safety direction` x  THEN `SFA penalty` OF 10000, 12, 0
    WHEN `removing a direction affixed to food premises` x   THEN `SFA penalty` OF 5000, 6, 0
    WHEN `refusing or mis-stating name and address`        THEN `SFA penalty` OF 300, 0, 0
    WHEN `contravening food regulations`                   THEN `SFA penalty` OF 5000, 0, 500
    OTHERWISE IF repeat THEN `SFA penalty` OF 10000, 3, 0 ELSE `SFA penalty` OF 5000, 0, 0

-- s 50(1): the Director-General "may compound any offence ... as may be
-- prescribed as being an offence that may be compounded by collecting ... a
-- sum of money not exceeding $1,000".
@ref s 50(1)
GIVEN prescribed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the most that may be collected to compound, prescribed:` prescribed MEANS
    IF prescribed THEN JUST 1000 ELSE NOTHING
